CommitDate: Mon Sep 28 18:21:27 2026 -0500

    fix: loud note + drift-probe corrupt finding on PyYAML-less rule mirror (TJ-DF-039)
    
    On a host without PyYAML, rules.py's JSON fallback is the ONLY path a .yaml
    rule file can take (YAML is not JSON), so the shipped mirror loaded ZERO
    rules, silently — and scripts/rules-drift-probe.py printed a bare WARNING
    followed by "RESULT: drift=0", exit 0. The tool whose job is catching a
    broken mirror called the broken mirror clean (fresh Debian agent dogfood,
    docs/dogfood/2026-09-28-fresh-install-smoke).
    
    - rules.py: when the JSON fallback cannot parse the file, emit one loud
      stderr note naming the file and the cause (TJ-GAP-070 note style), record
      it in RuleLoader.parse_notes, then re-raise. _load_file keeps its fail-open
      behaviour: the engine's ACTION is unchanged, only the silence is removed.
    - rules-drift-probe.py: an unparseable installed rule file is now a
      first-class finding — RESULT carries corrupt=N, the WARNING names the file
      and states its rules are NOT loaded, a NOTE names the remedy (install
      python3-yaml), and --fail-on-drift exits 1 when corrupt > 0. A bare run
      still exits 0 (classifier discipline); docstring and --help updated.
    - tests: +6 in plugin/test_rules_drift_probe.py (corrupt counted in RESULT,
      bare exit 0, --fail-on-drift exit 1, a real DRIFT row not masked, clean
      host corrupt=0, in-process counts), +4 in plugin/test_bridge_fail_closed.py
      (PyYAML-less mirror note + zero rules, with-PyYAML control on the same
      file, unchanged BLOCK verdict, JSON-document fallback still loads).
    
    Full suite: .venv/bin/python -m pytest -x --tb=short -> 1507 passed, 7
    skipped. ruff check + ruff format --check clean.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
